      "id": 1,
      "text": "In 1901, Blevins opened a post office that carried the name of local pioneer Hugh A. Blevins.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.blevinsarhistory.com/town-origins",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Prescott & Northwestern railroad built a stop in Blevins, letting the Ozan Lumber Company ship lumber, crops, and cotton from the town’s gin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.blevinsarhistory.com/town-origins",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Blevins was officially incorporated on September 10, 1914, giving the community its legal status.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.blevinsarhistory.com/town-origins",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early settlers chose land two miles north of Marlbrook, where Hempstead County’s first courthouse once stood.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.blevinsarhistory.com/town-origins",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
